{
  "_comment": "Decoded store payloads reduced to the fields the block reads. Apple field names follow JWSTransactionDecodedPayload and responseBodyV2DecodedPayload; Google field names follow ProductPurchaseV2 and the real-time developer notification messages. Signatures are not included: tests inject these as the output of the signature and API verification step, and test signature failure separately with a real library and a tampered token. Timestamps: Apple purchaseDate, revocationDate and signedDate are epoch milliseconds.",
  "_usage": "Identifiers are placeholders: bundle `com.example.acmegame`, package `com.example.acmegame`, products `acme_*`, accounts `account-001` and `account-002`. The account tokens are UUIDs mapped in `account_tokens` (with STORE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN_SOURCE = account_id each token equals its account id; these test accounts use the wallet_token mode so that ids like account-001 can stay readable). Clock 2026-10-27T12:00:00Z. `expected_plans` gives the output of planPurchase (backend.md section 6) for each payload.",
